cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NEBULA in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "NEBULA: a language-independent specification for opaque rotating refresh tokens"
abstract: >-
  A precise, language-independent specification of the RFC 9700 refresh-token
  model — opaque selector/verifier tokens, rotation on every use, replay
  detection with family revocation, bounded lifetimes and optional sender
  binding — together with ten conformant reference implementations and a
  conformance suite published as machine-readable data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Teodori
    given-names: Matteo
    # The contact of record, shared with the package manifests and the paper.
    # SUPPORT.md says what each address is for.
    email: hello@nebulatoken.dev
version: 1.0.2
# Must equal the date of the release named by `version` above, together with
# that release's heading in CHANGELOG.md. scripts/version.mjs checks all three;
# RELEASING.md carries the step that keeps them in step.
date-released: "2026-08-04"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nebula-token/nebula-token"
url: "https://nebulatoken.dev"
keywords:
  - refresh-token
  - token-rotation
  - replay-detection
  - authentication
  - oauth2
  - rfc9700
  - security
  - conformance-testing
#
# The paper is posted, so the block that was reserved for it below is now real:
# citing tools prefer `preferred-citation` over the software record above, which
# is the intent — cite the paper, and get the software through it.
#
# `journal:` is deliberately absent. CFF 1.2.0 has no `preprint` reference type,
# and the usual workaround is `type: article` with `journal: arXiv` — but arXiv
# is a preprint server, not a journal, and this file is read by tools that
# render that field verbatim into a reference list. `type: article` with a DOI,
# a URL and a `notes` line that says what it is states the same thing without
# claiming a venue that does not exist.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "NEBULA: A Language-Independent Specification for Opaque Rotating Refresh Tokens"
  authors:
    - family-names: Teodori
      given-names: Matteo
      email: hello@nebulatoken.dev
  year: 2026
  month: 8
  doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2608.04115
  url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.04115"
  identifiers:
    - type: other
      value: "arXiv:2608.04115v1"
      description: The arXiv identifier, including the version this entry describes.
  notes: Preprint, posted to arXiv (cs.CR) on 2026-08-04. Not peer-reviewed.
#
# An archival DOI is still deliberately absent: it is minted from a published
# tag, and RELEASING.md carries that as a post-tag step. Note that the DOI above
# is arXiv's own, for the paper — it is not an archive of this repository at the
# version named above, and the two must not be conflated. The shape the archival
# one takes when it arrives:
#
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#     description: Archived snapshot of the release named by `version` above.
